  "notes": [
    "F08-2: the billing admission runs OUTSIDE the limiter in the middleware chain, so a fail-closed limiter refusal still writes an execution row plus a reservation and a release entry per refused request. No money is held, but a Redis outage produces PostgreSQL churn on the money path."
